    <statement><p>Given that <m>f(5) = -1</m> and <m>f'(5) = -5</m>, approximate
<m>f(4.7)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(4.7) \approx</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Using the formula, <m>f(c + h) \approx f(c) + f'(c)\cdot h</m>,
<me>f(4.7) = f(5  - 0.3) \approx f(5) + f'(5)\cdot (-0.3)
  = -1  - 5 \cdot (-0.3) = 0.5.</me>


</solution>
